MurMur audio_quality.py is a new Python implementation informed by TypeFree
audioManager.ts analyzeVoiceActivity/prepareAudioForTranscription and Rust
commands/audio_quality.rs. It uses conservative fixed RMS silence screening,
20ms frames and generous lead/tail trimming, not AI denoising or semantic VAD.
Thresholds differ: default RMS floor 0.001; no percentile noise multiplier;
gate is opt-in at half the fixed threshold. Original PCM is preserved for
opt-in recording export. No idle microphone/pre-keypress ring buffer exists.
